# Normalize line endings on checkout.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: scripts/check-app-claims.mjs pins a SHA-256 of its own source
# in docs/design/osl-public-claim-allowlist.md as tamper evidence. GitHub's
# windows-latest runners check out with core.autocrlf=true, so every LF became
# CRLF, the bytes changed, and the digest could NEVER match on CI:
#   "Claim-gate source contract mismatch: expected 251c1268..., actual 45e266b3..."
# It reproduced on any PR, not just one. Without a committed eol policy a
# content-addressed gate is unpinnable across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely require CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.msi binary
